    {
      "text": "utter things which have been kept secret, Matt. 13:35. wilt enter into life, keep the commandments, Matt. 19:17. that ye may keep your own tradition, Mark 7:9. Mary kept all these things, and pondered, Luke 2:19. having heard the word, keep it, and bring forth fruit, Luke 8:15. they kept it close, and told no man, Luke 9:36. they that hear the word of God, and keep it, Luke 11:28. If a man keep my saying, he shall never see death, John 8:51 (8:52). If ye love me, keep my commandments, John 14:15 (D&C 42:29). If a man love me, he will keep my words, John 14:23. even as I have kept my Father’s commandments, John 15:10. Father, keep through thine own name those … given me, John 17:11. keep them from the evil, John 17:15. received the law … and have not kept it, Acts 7:53. command them to keep the law of Moses, Acts 15:5. keep themselves from things offered to idols, Acts 21:25. I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection, 1 Cor. 9:27. keep the ordinances, as I delivered them, 1 Cor. 11:2. Endeavouring to keep the unity of the Spirit, Eph. 4:3. peace of God … shall keep your hearts and minds, Philip. 4:7. stablish you, and keep you from evil, 2 Thes. 3:3. keep that which is committed to thy trust, 1 Tim. 6:20. keep by the Holy Ghost which dwelleth in us, 2 Tim. 1:14. finished my course, I have kept the faith, 2 Tim. 4:7. keep himself unspotted from the world, James 1:27. keep the whole law, and yet offend in one point, James 2:10. kept by the power of God through faith, 1 Pet. 1:5. heavens and the earth … by the same word are kept in store, 2 Pet. 3:7. we know him, if we keep his commandments, 1 Jn. 2:3. receive of him, because we keep his commandments, 1 Jn. 3:22. Keep yourselves in the love of God, Jude 1:21. keep those things which are written, Rev. 1:3. kept the word of my patience, I also will keep, Rev. 3:10.",
